From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:37:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: stmpe: Remove the IRQ domain after the child devices

stmpe_remove() removes the IRQ domain before mfd_remove_devices(), so the
children still hold interrupts from the domain when they go away, and
their free_irq() deactivates the interrupt through the freed domain:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000040
  pc : __irq_domain_deactivate_irq+0x30/0x7c
  Call trace:
   __irq_domain_deactivate_irq+0x30/0x7c (P)
   irq_domain_deactivate_irq+0x34/0x58
   free_irq+0x1a8/0x33c
   devm_irq_release+0x28/0x3c
   ...
   platform_device_unregister+0x3c/0xc0
   mfd_remove_devices_fn+0xe4/0x108 [mfd_core]
   ...
   stmpe_remove+0x68/0x80 [stmpe]
   stmpe_i2c_remove+0x24/0x38 [stmpe_i2c]

The parent interrupt has the same problem: it is devm-managed, so it is
only freed after stmpe_remove() returns, and its handler looks up the
child interrupts in the domain until then.

Remove the domain from a devm action added right after it is created.
devres runs it after the driver's remove callback has removed the
children and, in reverse order, after the parent interrupt is freed. It
also disposes of the mappings that mfd_add_devices() created, which
irq_domain_remove() expects to be gone, and covers the probe error paths,
where the domain was left behind.

Seen on a Galaxy Tab S3, whose keyboard cover carries an STMPE1801 that
is removed whenever the cover is taken off: the second removal, with a
key held, oopsed as above.

Fixes: 57bf2a312ab2 ("mfd: stmpe: Remove IRQ domain upon removal")
Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/mfd/stmpe.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c b/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c
index 2fc28708d2c7..974108cf9384 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c
@@ -1219,6 +1219,17 @@ static const struct irq_domain_ops stmpe_irq_ops = {
         .xlate  = irq_domain_xlate_twocell,
 };
 
+static void stmpe_irq_remove(void *data)
+{
+	struct stmpe *stmpe = data;
+	irq_hw_number_t hwirq;
+
+	for (hwirq = 0; hwirq < stmpe->variant->num_irqs; hwirq++)
+		irq_dispose_mapping(irq_find_mapping(stmpe->domain, hwirq));
+
+	irq_domain_remove(stmpe->domain);
+}
+
 static int stmpe_irq_init(struct stmpe *stmpe, struct device_node *np)
 {
 	int base = 0;
@@ -1231,7 +1242,12 @@ static int stmpe_irq_init(struct stmpe *stmpe, struct device_node *np)
 		return -ENOSYS;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	/*
+	 * Released after stmpe_remove() has removed the child devices and,
+	 * as it is added before the parent interrupt is requested, after
+	 * that interrupt is freed, so nothing uses the domain any more.
+	 */
+	return devm_add_action_or_reset(stmpe->dev, stmpe_irq_remove, stmpe);
 }
 
 static int stmpe_chip_init(struct stmpe *stmpe)
@@ -1508,9 +1524,6 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(stmpe_probe);
 
 void stmpe_remove(struct stmpe *stmpe)
 {
-	if (stmpe->domain)
-		irq_domain_remove(stmpe->domain);
-
 	__stmpe_disable(stmpe, STMPE_BLOCK_ADC);
 
 	mfd_remove_devices(stmpe->dev);
-- 
2.56.0

